 "how": "equation (3), the bijection between the spaces X_delta (a constant times Q in the tail, plus decaying) and Y_delta,0 (decaying, orthogonal to Q). Main's reading: the argument is the standard one for a Laplace-type operator on a finite-area cusp between weighted Hoelder spaces with the constant asymptote adjoined, and its channel-by-channel steps hold exactly (record physical-c3e-02). It is conditional on what main has not checked: that the background is exactly parallel on the whole cusp end, so that the operator separates into constant-coefficient channels; that the global kernel is exactly Q (the lane derives it from its earlier files, not yet read); the uniform estimate over angular frequencies in the presence of the first-order angular drift; and the Schauder and core-matching steps, which are standard and are stated, not written out. No lemma has been found to fail",
